From 96d5ca3efcd00dfa7f33c8f770c8ed2c1c1a9fe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 02:14:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cassette kernel/capability split: domain-blind kernel +
 opt-in capability modules

KERNEL (every cassette, every industry): identity, typed parameter
declarations, judge(episode) -> QualityResult with cassette-owned
cutoffs, explain(episode) -> factor-level reasons, and a CAPABILITIES
manifest. Kernel-required parameters: governance_trigger only.

CAPABILITIES (opt-in, each owns its parameters and methods):
- telephony_ingest: twilio_* thresholds, long_wait_threshold,
  score_outcome_quality / diagnose_abandonment / get_friction_thresholds
- routing_topology: get_queue_definitions / _infer_intent_to_label
- rl: compute_reward
- self_healing: get_healing_bounds, expected_wait_bounds

Load-time validation (schema 2.0.0) checks kernel + union of enabled
capabilities, verifies enabled capabilities' methods exist, and
REJECTS any declared parameter owned by a disabled capability (the
anti-placeholder rule). Snapshots record the manifest.

episode.py: kernel ground-truth record. Invariants enforced at
validation, before any judgment path: (1) a reason is owed on ANY
requested-vs-actual mismatch -- paid-but-reduced counts, not just
formal denials; (2) actor self-report is cross-checked against the
observed record (twin posture) and never read by judgment;
divergences are prepended to every explanation.

IVR: reference implementation, all four capabilities, judge proven
arithmetically identical to score_outcome_quality (equivalence sweep).
Banking: routing + rl + self_healing; placeholder twilio thresholds
removed; judgment moved to kernel surface, arithmetic unchanged;
refused at the door by telephony pipelines (SentinelCore, harnesses,
Twilio ingest all guard at construction). Both cassettes 2.0.0: code
hash changed, binding enforcement requires a new version identity.

Pre-existing defect fixed: serialize_cassette_for_ledger duplicated
snapshot serialization and had drifted; now delegates to
GovernanceParameters.snapshot().

Tests: 307 passed (279 baseline + 28 new), including a kernel-only
cassette with zero telephony surface that loads, validates, and
judges episodes.
